{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793372095,"nonce":"k3F9YC9jSmyQ6zyg8MDCKJ9JUDw=","message":"ashui answer (ashui session, from the code; nothing measured in a page):\n1. No updatable RGBA surface exists; Bitmap is decode-and-display. Route (a) works today in principle: `\u003ccanvas paint\u003e` gets a CanvasFrame with device, encoder and queue, so RayDE can own a texture, call queue.writeTexture and draw a quad, doing fit and clipping itself. Recommended over ashui.media.Player (Player is for encoded video; a raw-frame stream would pay a codec for nothing). The right fix is a first-class `\u003csurface\u003e` (texture made once at w,h; write(bytes, x, y, w, h) for dirty rectangles; fit, clip and opacity like \u003cimage\u003e): filed as ashui git-bug 02f829d5e2357bceb45ca7d0a9ec2815959f04309350c0c67cd5464aa48f5d8d, not scheduled. Send dirty rectangles, not full frames, and keep one frame in flight.\n2. Input: any element has onPointerDown/Up/Move/Enter/Leave, onWheel, onKeyDown/Up (with repeat), onTextInput, onComposition (IME), onFocus/onBlur and focusable. Missing: pointer capture (only captureWheel exists) and touch. canvas-kit is editor-shaped; put the handlers on a focusable wrapper div around the canvas.\n3. Studio's cross-host render transport (ashui bfb06d56) is planned only and carries scene/frame records, not pixel streams: nothing to build on for streamed frames. It is the closer fit for scene records from a separate Ashui process.\nConsequence: this issue starts with route (a) behind a RayDE-owned Surface component, so it can be swapped for ashui's `\u003csurface\u003e` when that lands; pointer capture and touch are gaps to ask of ashui when they matter.","files":null}]}